DO NOT (binding for future agents)
-----------------------------------

1. DO NOT default-flip `JPEG_LEVER_A_ENABLE` to ON. Measurement
   is conclusive: +8.57pp regression on the 200-file bench. The
   structural problem is the merged single-context Huffman code
   cannot match the per-context tightness of the gradient/left/zero
   predictor split on CFL/QF/ACS/EPF tokens, even when most values
   are 0.
2. DO NOT respawn lever B with use_global_tree=true expecting big
   gains. Measured upper bound is ~10 B/file = ~2 KB on 200 files
   = ~0.005pp. The required refactor (moving qtable encoding from
   per-stream tree to the global tree) is multi-day work for sub-
   noise gain.
3. DO NOT respawn lever C for YCbCr JPEGs. The libjxl field
   visitor reads `Bool(false, &alternate)` when xyb_encoded=false,
   and YCbCr forces alternate=1 ≠ default 0. Structurally
   impossible. Lever C could ONLY apply to RGB (non-YCbCr) JPEGs
   which are extremely rare in the bench corpus.
4. DO NOT respawn lever D thinking selectors might differ.
   Verified bit-identical via libjxl `entropy_coder.h:37-42` direct
   read.
5. DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any future JPEG byte movement
   (per CLAUDE.md W44-66 user correction). JPEG transcode is
   integer arithmetic end-to-end.
6. DO NOT remove the JPEG_SECTION_DUMP probe. It's load-bearing
   diagnostic infrastructure for future investigators, zero cost
   when the env var is unset.

Follow-on candidates (NOT in this session's scope)
---------------------------------------------------

1. **Section-level cjxl-vs-ours bit comparison** — instrument cjxl
   (via libjxl AuxOut) to dump per-section bytes, then bit-compare
   against our JPEG_SECTION_DUMP output. Would isolate which
   section absorbs the remaining +1.52pp. ~1 day to wire up.
2. **Merge qtable stream into global tree** (lever B variant).
   Multi-day port (move from per-stream tree to global tree, ensure
   global tree has qtable-compatible leaf). Upper bound ~10 B/file.
3. **AC stream histogram clustering** — try `kBest` (full pair-
   merge) for JPEG instead of `kFast`. cjxl uses kFast at effort
   7; libjxl `effort >= 9` (kTortoise) uses kBest. Worth trying
   since AC stream histogram serialization is ~40 bytes/histogram
   × 116 histograms = 4.6 KB/file = substantial. Risk: encode time
   blowup.
4. **Approach the +1.52pp problem from the codestream-layout side**
   — try emitting the JPEG-mode frame with different group sizes
   (current is 256x256, libjxl might use larger groups for JPEG).

